#: src/workspace-trust.md:1
msgid "Workspace trust"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:3
msgid "Helix has several features that can execute arbitrary code:"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:5
msgid "Language servers (LSP)"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:6
msgid "Debug adapters (DAP)"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:7
msgid ""
"Local workspace configuration (`.helix/config.toml`, `.helix/languages.toml`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:8
msgid ""
"Git integration (filters and other commands in a repository's `.git/config`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:10
msgid ""
"To protect against malicious projects (a checked-out PR, a freshly cloned "
"repository, etc.) Helix gates these behind explicit per-workspace trust. By "
"default language servers start automatically (their binaries come from "
"`$PATH`, not from the workspace) and debug adapters may be launched, but "
"loading `.helix/config.toml` or `.helix/languages.toml` and trusting a "
"repository's `.git/config` requires opting in. Note that debug adapters are "
"never started automatically — you launch them yourself — but the same trust "
"level still gates whether they may run. The model is intentionally similar "
"to [direnv](https://direnv.net/): you run `:workspace-trust` once per "
"workspace and Helix remembers across sessions."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:21
msgid "Granting trust"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:23
msgid ""
"When Helix opens a file inside a workspace it has never seen before, a modal "
"trust prompt asks:"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:26
msgid "**Trust** — allow the workspace permanently."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:27
msgid "**Never** — exclude the workspace; never prompt again."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:29
msgid ""
"`<Esc>` (or any other dismissal) caches \"untrusted for this session\" so "
"the prompt doesn't re-fire for every file you open in the workspace. The "
"next time you start Helix in that workspace, it'll prompt again."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:33
msgid ""
"A small `[⚠]` indicator appears in the bottom-right of the editor (next to "
"the macro-recording `[@]`) whenever the workspace is in restricted mode "
"_and_ running `:workspace-trust` would change observable behavior — i.e. "
"when there's a local config to load or an LSP that would start."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:38
msgid ""
"You can also run `:workspace-trust` / `:workspace-untrust` / `:workspace-"
"exclude` directly from the typed command prompt."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:41
msgid "Revoking trust"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:43
msgid ""
"Run `:workspace-untrust` to revoke a workspace's trust grant. The next time "
"you open a file in that workspace, you're back to the untrusted hint."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:46
msgid "Detecting changes after trust was granted"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:48
msgid ""
"When you trust a workspace, Helix records a hash of every file under `.helix/"
"`. If those files change afterwards (a malicious checkout, an inadvertent "
"rebase, etc.) Helix detects the mismatch on the next open and reports the "
"workspace as _stale_:"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:58
msgid ""
"In the stale state, language servers continue to run (they use the globally-"
"configured binaries on `$PATH`, which are unchanged), but `.helix/config."
"toml` and `.helix/languages.toml` are not loaded. Run `:workspace-trust` "
"again to re-pin the new hash."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:63
msgid "Storage"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:65
msgid ""
"Trust grants live in `data_dir()/workspace_trust/`, one small file per "
"workspace. The filename is the SHA-256 of the workspace's absolute path; the "
"contents look like:"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:75
msgid "Linux, macOS: `~/.local/share/helix/workspace_trust/`"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:76
msgid "Windows: `%AppData%\\Roaming\\helix\\workspace_trust\\`"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:78
msgid ""
"The one-file-per-workspace shape is safe under multiple concurrent Helix "
"instances — different workspaces never write the same file."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:81
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:83
msgid "Settings live under `[editor.workspace-trust]`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:85
msgid "Key"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:85
msgid "Values"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:85
msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:85
msgid "Effect"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:87
msgid "`level`"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:87
msgid "`\"none\"`, `\"servers\"`, `\"insecure\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:87
msgid "`\"servers\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:87
msgid "What is auto-trusted in every workspace. See below."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:88
msgid "`prompt`"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:88
msgid "`true`, `false`"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:88
msgid "`true`"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:88
msgid ""
"Whether to surface the modal popup. The `[⚠]` indicator is shown regardless."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:89
msgid "`trusted`"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:89
msgid "list of glob patterns"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:89
msgid "`[]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:89
msgid ""
"Workspaces matching a pattern are trusted without a grant. Discouraged; see "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:91
msgid "Recommended setups"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:93
msgid "**Default: trust servers, prompt before loading workspace config.**"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:95
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[editor.workspace-trust]\n"
"level = \"servers\"\n"
"prompt = true\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:101
msgid ""
"Language servers start automatically in every workspace — their binaries "
"come from `$PATH` and are not workspace-controlled — and debug adapters you "
"launch are allowed to run. The modal only appears when opening a file in a "
"workspace whose `.helix/config.toml` or `.helix/languages.toml` would unlock "
"something. Trust everything else with one keystroke per workspace, deny with "
"another."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:108
msgid "**Maximum security: never prompt, trust each workspace by hand.**"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:110
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[editor.workspace-trust]\n"
"level = \"none\"\n"
"prompt = false\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:116
msgid ""
"Nothing trusts implicitly: language servers, debug adapters, local config, "
"and git `Trust::Full` are all off until you run `:workspace-trust`. The "
"popup never appears; the `[⚠]` indicator in the bottom-right is your only "
"signal that the current workspace is restricted. Suited to users who would "
"rather grant trust as a deliberate action than dismiss a dialog."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:123
msgid ""
"\\[!WARNING\\] `level = \"insecure\"` is highly discouraged. It implicitly "
"trusts every workspace you open, which defeats the protection entirely: a "
"checked-out PR with a malicious `.helix/config.toml` would get its "
"configuration loaded and any language server it defines launched, with no "
"prompt and no indicator. Only set this if you accept full responsibility for "
"what's in every project directory you `cd` into."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:131
msgid "Trusting workspaces by path (discouraged)"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:133
msgid ""
"If you keep all your repositories under a predictable layout, you can trust "
"them in bulk with glob patterns instead of granting each workspace "
"individually:"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:137
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[editor.workspace-trust]\n"
"trusted = [\n"
"  \"~/src/github.com/me/*\",\n"
"  \"~/work/repos/*\",\n"
"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:145
msgid ""
"A workspace whose path matches a pattern is trusted for everything, just as "
"if you had run `:workspace-trust` in it. `~` and environment variables are "
"expanded."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:149
msgid ""
"\\[!WARNING\\] This is weaker than an explicit grant and is discouraged. It "
"skips the `.helix/` change detection entirely (a malicious checkout under a "
"matched directory is never flagged as stale), and it trusts _any_ repository "
"that later lands under a matching path — including one you clone into `~/src/"
"github.com/me/` from an untrusted source. Prefer granting trust per "
"workspace; reach for this only if the prompts are genuinely disruptive to "
"your workflow. An explicit `:workspace-exclude` still overrides a matching "
"pattern."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:159
msgid "Git trust"
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:161
msgid ""
"Workspace trust also gates how Helix opens git repositories. Untrusted "
"workspaces are opened in [gix](https://github.com/Byron/gitoxide)'s `Trust::"
"Reduced` mode; trusted workspaces use `Trust::Full`."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:165
msgid ""
"Under `Trust::Reduced`, gix still runs the full filter pipeline (so built-in "
"conversions like `core.autocrlf` keep working) but ignores configuration "
"coming from the untrusted, repository-local `.git/config`. That means "
"`filter.*.clean` / `filter.*.smudge` drivers and similar keys that would "
"otherwise execute external programs are dropped until you trust the "
"workspace."
msgstr ""

#: src/workspace-trust.md:172
msgid ""
"Helix forces this trust level explicitly rather than letting gix infer it "
"from `.git` directory ownership — a malicious `.git/config` in a directory "
"you happen to own is still treated as untrusted until you run `:workspace-"
"trust`."
msgstr ""
